---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>About Alessandro Paravano | Space Economy &amp; Complex Infrastructures</title>
  <meta name="description" content="About Alessandro Paravano, Assistant Professor at Politecnico di Milano researching the Space Economy, complex infrastructures, value networks, systems architecting and project governance." />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />

  <meta property="og:type" content="profile" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="About Alessandro Paravano | Space Economy & Complex Infrastructures" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Assistant Professor at Politecnico di Milano researching the Space Economy, complex infrastructures, value networks, systems architecting and project governance." />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
  <meta property="profile:first_name" content="Alessandro" />
  <meta property="profile:last_name" content="Paravano" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(profilePageSchema)}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)}></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <nav class="container site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Alessandro Paravano</a>
      <div class="navlinks">
        <a href="/research/">Research</a>
        <a href="/publications/">Publications</a>
        <a href="/about/" aria-current="page">About</a>
        <a href="/media-contact/">Media &amp; Contact</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="about-page">
    <section class="container about-page-hero">
      <div class="about-hero-title">
        <p class="about-eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Alessandro Paravano</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="about-hero-copy">
        <p class="about-role">Assistant Professor, Politecnico di Milano</p>
        <p class="about-hero-statement">Researching how the Space Economy and complex infrastructures evolve through new technologies, ecosystems, value networks, systems architecting and changing forms of governance.</p>
        <div class="about-hero-links" aria-label="Primary academic profiles">
          <a href="https://www.som.polimi.it/en/faculty/paravano-alessandro/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">POLIMI</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?view_op=list_works&hl=it&user=ZLy7CJAAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">Google Scholar</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6884-3712" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">ORCID</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alessandroparavano/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="profile-heading">
      <div class="container about-section-grid">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <h2 id="profile-heading">Profile</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-section-content about-prose">
          <p>Alessandro Paravano is an Assistant Professor and Core Faculty member at the School of Management of Politecnico di Milano, where he also conducts research with the Space Economy Observatory. His work examines how the space industry is changing as new technologies, private actors, markets and governance arrangements reshape the relationships between space infrastructure and its users.</p>
          <p>His research connects management and engineering perspectives to understand how complex projects and infrastructures create economic, social and environmental value across networks of organizations and end users. The Space Economy is his primary empirical domain, complemented by research on other complex, capital-intensive infrastructure systems.</p>
          <p>Across these settings, he studies business ecosystems and project ecologies, value and value networks, systems architecting, and project management and governance. His work combines qualitative and quantitative methods and is designed to connect rigorous research with decisions made by companies, public agencies and other organizations involved in complex projects.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-focus-section" aria-labelledby="focus-heading">
      <div class="container about-section-grid">
        <div class="about-section-heading">
          <h2 id="focus-heading">Research focus</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-section-content">
          <dl class="about-focus-list">
            <div>
              <dt>Primary domain</dt>
              <dd><strong>Space Economy</strong>, including the evolution of space markets, infrastructures, value chains and relationships between space and non-space sectors.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Space topics</dt>
              <dd>Earth Observation; GNSS, PNT and satellite navigation; satellite communications; commercial space stations and the LEO economy; space commercialization; governance, resilience and value creation.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Broader domain</dt>
              <dd><strong>Complex infrastructures</strong>, with research spanning space, energy and other long-lived, high-technology and capital-intensive infrastructure systems.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Research perspectives</dt>
              <dd>Business ecosystems and project ecologies; value and value networks; systems architecting; project management, organization and governance.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a class="about-inline-cta" href="/research/">Explore the research agenda →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
      <div class="container about-section-grid">
